<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key><string>com.jkrumm.warden-sweep</string>
  <!-- Folds a terminal sideclaw verdict onto the card the act-loop already wrote.
       Read-only against sideclaw; the only thing it mutates is the ledger and the
       card.

       Was gateway cron job 4dd759917dd1 ("Dispatch sweep", */5, no_agent: true).
       Promoting it removes the scheduling dependency on the gateway — the failure
       mode this repo exists for was ingest and verdict-folding running inside the
       process being supervised, which crash-looped seven times in 3m34s on
       2026-09-07 while the act-loop kept ticking against a ledger that had stopped
       receiving signals.

       Its cron wrapper (dispatch-sweep-cron.py) existed only to satisfy the gateway
       runner's contract — invoked with no args, stdout delivered as a Slack body —
       and is deleted with this move. Nothing is lost: the sweeper posts each verdict
       into its own origin thread directly and keeps stdout empty on purpose, so
       there was never a body to deliver. Diagnostics go to stderr, below.

       KNOWN GAP, recorded rather than hidden: the sweeper's delivery still shells out
       to ~/.local/bin/hermes send (dispatch-sweep.py:93), which does talk to the
       gateway. Scheduling is now independent; delivery is not yet. Moving it to the
       same plain-HTTP client the act-loop uses is tracked in STATE.md. -->
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>__HOME__/SourceRoot/warden/.venv/bin/python3</string>
    <string>__HOME__/SourceRoot/warden/scripts/dispatch-sweep.py</string>
  </array>
  <!-- 300s = the */5 the cron job ran on. Unchanged deliberately: the interval is
       what bounds how long a finished episode sits unfolded. -->
  <key>StartInterval</key><integer>300</integer>
  <key>RunAtLoad</key><true/>
  <key>StandardOutPath</key><string>__HOME__/Library/Logs/warden-sweep.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key><string>__HOME__/Library/Logs/warden-sweep.err</string>
</dict>
</plist>
